    "id": "prop:squires-rank-failure-full-domain",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "The chain, fork, and open star witnesses falsify the observational-context rank-selector conclusion of Squires et al., Appendix F.2, Proposition 10 on its full published model class, not merely on \\(\\mathcal M_p\\): under the normalized-mechanism embedding their context precisions, rank matrices, and scores are unchanged, while the true observational context is not a literal-score minimizer in the first chain, the fork, and the entire star region.  The natural symmetric score also fails, by a tie in the first chain and a strict error in the second.  This is a negative scope transfer only; the positive coordinate certificate is proved on the observed-coordinate fully covered class \\(\\mathcal M_p\\) and does not assert recovery under latent mixing.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "p",
      "M",
      "Cert"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "lem:squires-class-embedding",
      "lem:rank-witness-calculations",
      "thm:complete-certificate"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "By \\(\\texttt{lem:squires-class-embedding}\\), each legal witness in \\(\\mathcal M_p\\) is a point of the full Proposition-10 class, with \\(\\Theta_c=K_c\\) for every context.  Hence no rank or score changes under the embedding.  By \\(\\texttt{lem:rank-witness-calculations}\\), the first chain assigns literal score \\(3\\) to the observational context and score \\(2\\) to intervention contexts; the fork assigns the corresponding scores \\(5\\) and \\(4\\); and at every point of the nonempty open star region, (32) assigns \\(2p-1\\) to the observational context and \\(2p-2\\) to the root-intervention context.  In each case the observational context is not a minimizer, contradicting the asserted conclusion at points inside its published domain.  The same lemma gives symmetric scores \\((3,3,4)\\) for the first chain, so uniqueness fails, and \\((3,2,3)\\) for the second, so even minimization fails.\n\nThe embedding establishes only inclusion of \\(\\mathcal M_p\\) in the larger published class.  The positive invocation of \\(\\mathsf{Cert}\\) in \\(\\texttt{lem:rank-witness-calculations}\\) instead uses \\(\\texttt{thm:complete-certificate}\\), whose domain is \\(\\mathcal M_p\\).  Therefore the refutation transfers to the full class by restriction, whereas no positive certificate claim is made for models with nonidentity latent mixing.",
